  "summary": "Lineage-resolved and time-series scRNA-seq data now support models of developmental transitions beyond static snapshots.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread across most of these items is inferring how single-cell states change over time from scRNA-seq measurements. Lineage inpainting uses tree-structured transformers and stochastic interpolants to learn cell state dynamics across lineage context. Bowside, a shallow neural stochastic differentiation model, jointly infers single-cell trajectories and gene regulatory networks and is tested on hematopoiesis. BLOOM applies biologically informed conditional flow matching to generate developmental single-cell expression distributions across time, with benchmarking against 22 comparators. Deep Lineage, a published deep-learning method for time-series scRNA-seq with lineage tracing, predicts early fate biases and clone-level expression. What is new is the pairing of learned or mechanistic models with lineage context, gene regulatory structure, and biological constraints, rather than static snapshots alone.",
